{
  "note": "Every piece of gear the hero can wear. look.meshes are kit meshes (* = M_ or F_ for the body worn), look.forge are shapes built in actors/player/09f-gear-forge.js, look.cloth is simulated cloth (09g). look.hides names body regions the piece covers. stats: armor (max armour), hp, st (stamina), mana, dmg and spell (% bonus), speed (% move speed, can be negative). Weapons: dmg is a fraction (0.12 = +12%), reach multiplies sword range, affix is burn | leech | swift | slayer. Sword models (forge shape \"model\") are assets/character/weapons/<model>.glb, built by tools/character/build_weapons.mjs. Modelled armour: forge shape \"piece\" (assets/character/armor/<model>.glb; fit head | chest | shield, size, offset) and \"outfit\" with \"parts\" (skinned sets in assets/character/outfits/<id>.glb). Credits in THIRD_PARTY.md. ownSkirt: the piece has its own skirt, so cloth skirts from other gear are switched off. bulk: how far the piece stands off the body in metres, so capes hang outside it. ownSleeves: the piece has its own sleeves, so sleeved arm gear steps aside.",
  "testing": {
    "unlockAll": true,
    "why": "Every item is in the armoury from the first second, for play-testing. Set false to make gear drop-only."
